{
  "source": "Built for T-0190 and T-0189 (RQ-0173) from the Refund object, RefundListParams and the error object in the official stripe@23.1.0 type definitions (OpenAPI v2596; Refund.status pending | requires_action | succeeded | failed | canceled, Refund.created, failure_reason, failure_balance_transaction), in the shape of the T-0172 fixture (RQ-0163, RQ-0164). Not recorded from a live account: no Stripe key or network was available. lf-refund-v2-<refund id> is the document's first key; lf-refund-v3-<resend id> is a resend's recorded key (ADR-0091). No interaction answers a v2 create for a document Stripe already holds or for the 'vanished' document, and none answers a second create for the 'refused' one: they must never be requested. Security review r10 (2026-11-22): 'hung' (a create that lands after the cancel; no create is answered for the later document of the same credit) and 'mismatch' (a live refund of another amount). T-0208 (2026-11-23, RQ-0185): 'waiting' (nothing at Stripe; a resend is asked and left waiting, so the GET view shows it).",
  "apiVersion": "2026-10-28.endive",
  "accessed": "2026-11-16",
